From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Guo <shengchao.guo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:23:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 058/117] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: Derive TDM channels from DT
 mask

Derive the backend channel count of TDM DAIs from the cpu DAI TDM
slot mask in the DT, using the same DAI ID ranges and tx/rx mask
selection as q6tdm_set_tdm_slot(), so the channel count always matches
the number of slots programmed into the DSP. Each board then gets the
channel count its dai-link describes, e.g. 4/4 on Nord RRD, 6/4 on
RIDE. Keep the default of two when the link has no TDM slot
description, and fail the fixup on an invalid one.

Signed-off-by: Shawn Guo <shengchao.guo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Prasad Kumpatla <prasad.kumpatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261031082318.1146398-1-shengchao.guo@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>

[mzak: picked for q91o (21 Nov gains plan) from linux-next/maintainer tree commit 45e9d148a0a7; mark C: merged with our queued "run the TDM back ends at 32 bit, one channel per slot" case for the Q6 TDM ports (S32_LE, 8 channels unless the DT slot mask gives the count) to avoid a duplicate case]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 563c949220d27..2d6eb9a04f24f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -307,6 +307,40 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	channels->min = 2;
 	channels->max = 2;
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0 ... QUINARY_TDM_TX_7:
+	case AIF_TDM_RX_0 ... AIF_TDM_TX_12: {
+		struct qcom_snd_tdm_slot_cfg cpu_cfg, codec_cfg;
+		unsigned int mask;
+		int ret;
+
+		if (cpu_dai->id <= QUINARY_TDM_TX_7) {
+			/*
+			 * The TDM ports run 32-bit slots with every slot active
+			 * (dai-tdm-slot-*); codecs derive their slot length from
+			 * the stream width, and the DSP's TDM endpoint wants one
+			 * channel per active slot (8 unless the DT mask says
+			 * otherwise, below).
+			 */
+			snd_mask_none(fmt);
+			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
+			channels->min = 8;
+			channels->max = 8;
+		}
+
+		ret = qcom_snd_get_dai_tdm_slots(rtd, &cpu_cfg, &codec_cfg);
+		if (ret == -ENOENT)
+			break;
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		/* Same slot mask selection as q6tdm_set_tdm_slot() */
+		mask = (cpu_dai->id & 0x1) ? cpu_cfg.tx_mask : cpu_cfg.rx_mask;
+		if (mask) {
+			channels->min = hweight32(mask);
+			channels->max = channels->min;
+		}
+		break;
+	}
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
@@ -335,17 +369,6 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
 		}
 		break;
-	case PRIMARY_TDM_RX_0 ... QUINARY_TDM_TX_7:
-		/*
-		 * The TDM ports run 32-bit slots with every slot active (dai-tdm-slot-*);
-		 * codecs derive their slot length from the stream width, and the DSP's
-		 * TDM endpoint wants one channel per active slot.
-		 */
-		snd_mask_none(fmt);
-		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
-		channels->min = 8;
-		channels->max = 8;
-		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
